From ef430a4551ab7dd2882a9b91e7483e24d3b05559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:15:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/21] Vizzbox 1.0, tests: counter-check, fuzzer, old firmware
 on a unit with favourites, the heaviest drop

tests/vizzbox_mutants.py: 22 deliberate faults in the producer, its ISR part, its screen, the autosave hook
and 2 in the installer, each caught by the test that should see it (tests/vizz_mutants.py stays for Vizz
2.0's). tests/vizzbox_fuzz.c: the VIZZBOX's knobs, buttons, keys, favourites, modes, MENU, MIDI in and power
cycles at random under ASan / UBSan; no hanging note, every voice free after STOP, a fresh device plays (with
a clock from outside where the MENU was left on USB or TRS clock). tests/vizzbox_compat.c: a unit with
favourites booted, loaded, saved and autosaved by Skiff 2.0.1 and Vizz 2.0 (their trees from git): the
favourites untouched, all of it there again on the Vizzbox; tests/ldr_test.c: the favourites kept over an
update. tests/vizzbox_inactive.c: the GROOVEBOX with the producer compiled in plays as without it, audio,
MIDI and screen bit for bit. tests/vizzbox_budget.c: every subgenre's first DROP at ENERGY and VARIATION 100
against Skiff's heavy song (CPU time side by side; the heaviest 0.6..0.8x over several runs, with every
effect 0.65..0.75x against the heavy song with them), at most 8 voices, none stolen. tests/producer_test.c: the user's projects, autosave and
pattern pool untouched by a producer session and back after off and on; a favourite saved while playing
written once stopped; CC 104 0 into the GROOVEBOX on a unit that never played; song N runs subgenre N only.
web/emu/make_vizzbox_emu.py, test_vizzbox_emu.mjs: the Vizzbox in the browser as one file, tested in
Chromium from the disk. producer.c: vb_note, never called, removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R1rawnvCsrvDZVbc37ZFUY
